hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1571","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Maryam Al-Masry told us, my grandfather told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told me, he told me Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that he heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr on the pulpit saying to the people: “If one of you enters the mosque and the people are bowing, Let him kneel when he enters, then let him kneel until he enters the row, for that is the Sunnah.” Ataa said: I saw him do that."
